# UI atomic architecture (`packages/ui/src/patterns`)

## Capitalization (consistent naming)

- **React components** — **PascalCase** for every word. **Hero band** — **`ReadBootBand`** with **`surface`** (boxed vs open); presets **`BoxedFeatureHero`**, **`FullBleedHero`**. Also: `BlogCard`, `ConnectFooterSection`. Do not use `camelCase`, `snake_case`, or **partial** PascalCase for component names.

- **File names** — Match the **primary symbol**: `BoxedFeatureHero.tsx`, `FullBleedHero.module.scss`, etc. Folder names use the same (**PascalCase**), e.g. `Organisms/Hero/BoxedFeatureHero.tsx` or `Molecules/Cards/BlogCard/BlogCard.tsx`.

- **Props / types** — **PascalCase** + `Props` suffix where applicable: `FullBleedHeroProps`. Type aliases follow the same rule.

- **Non-module SCSS partials** (shared mixins, no CSS Modules class export) — **kebab-case** with leading underscore when shared: `_hero-shared.scss`, `_section-shell.scss`.

- **CSS Module class names** — **camelCase** inside `*.module.scss` (e.g. `.portraitFrame`, `.ctaRow`) unless an existing file already uses a different BEM-style; **stay consistent within a file**.

- **Exports from `index.tsx` barrels** — Re-export names must match **PascalCase** component names; avoid introducing alternate casings for the same component.

## Layers

- **Atoms** — primitives (buttons, typography, tokens, `SectionLayout`).
- **Molecules** — composed chunks (cards, nav pieces, **reusable layout grids**).
- **Organisms** — full sections (heroes, bordered content blocks, **footer strips**, card grids).
- **Templates** — **only** page composition: order sections, pass props, thin wrappers. **No** long-lived marketing copy in the template file; defaults live in modules or apps.

## README in each component folder

- Every **component directory** (the folder that owns the primary `*.tsx`) includes a **`README.md`**: **import** (`@repo/ui/atoms` / `molecules` / `organisms` / `templates`, or `@repo/ui/patterns/...` when not on a barrel), **when to use**, **Storybook** colocation, and pointers to workspace rules (linking, branding) as needed.

## Naming: shape-first (layout)

Use **layout/shape** names for **reusable** blocks whose primary contract is **silhouette** (grid, split columns, timeline, billboard headline):

- Examples: `BoxedFeatureHero`, `FullBleedHero`, `TwoColumnCalloutSection`, `VisionRoadmapSection`, `TitledCardGrid` (exact names evolve).
- **SCSS:** shared partials under the same folder (e.g. `Organisms/Hero/_hero-shared.scss`) per variant pair; **module** SCSS per component (`*.module.scss`).

## Naming: domain / role (not shape)

Do **not** force shape-only names for:

- **Cards** tied to a use case (`BlogCard`, `ProjectCard`, future spotlight cards) — shapes may change; name reflects **content + use**.
- **Navigation** (`NavigationBar`, `NavigationMenu`, `NavigationLink`).

- **Branding** (`LogoImage`, `LogoImageClient`).

- **Typography** and **color/token** stories — semantic or reference names.

- **Footer / connect strips** — **landmark role** (`ConnectFooterSection`, etc.) over abstract shape.

- **Theme / alerts** — behavior or intent.

## Data

- Apps or CMS **assemble props** at the route/page layer. Package **defaults** may exist for Storybook and fallbacks; avoid treating defaults as the only production source.

## Imports

- Cross-package: **public exports** only (`@repo/ui/atoms`, `@repo/ui/molecules`, `@repo/ui/organisms`, `@repo/ui/templates`). No deep `src/` imports across packages.

## Editorial copy (docs, Storybook, markdown)

- For **human-facing** descriptions of layout and hierarchy, prefer **newspaper terminology** in **`readboot-newspaper-terminology.mdc`** (kicker, deck, lead, boxed, full-bleed, rule). **PascalCase code names** stay as defined above.

## Layout model (surface × grid × slots)

- **Target architecture** for heroes, sections, and showcases: **`readboot-layout-model.mdc`** (unified bands, boxed/open prop, showcases as repeating card + data, types placement, migration table).

## Atomic inventory (which atom type per band)

- **Band-by-band** breakdown with **Branding / Interactive / LayoutAtoms / …**: **`readboot-atomic-layout-inventory.mdc`**.
